{"id":"s1.2.7","slug":"multiplying-two-numbers-near-100","title":"Multiplying Two Numbers Near 100","content":"<p class=\"mb-4\">This trick simplifies multiplying two numbers that are close to 100 (or 1000, etc.).</p><ul class=\"list-disc pl-6 space-y-2 mb-4\"><li><strong>Both numbers over 100:</strong> For $103 \\times 108$, the last two digits are the product of the differences from 100 ($3 \\times 8 = 24$). The first part of the answer is one number plus the other's difference from 100 ($103+8=111$). Answer: 11124.</li><li><strong>Both numbers under 100:</strong> For $97 \\times 94$, the last two digits are the product of the differences from 100 ($3 \\times 6 = 18$). The first part is one number minus the other's difference from 100 ($97-6=91$). Answer: 9118.</li><li><strong>One over, one under 100:</strong> For $103 \\times 94$, the last two digits are $100 - (3 \\times 6) = 82$. The first part is the larger number, minus the smaller's difference from 100, minus 1 ($103-6-1=96$). Answer: 9682.</li></ul>","summary":"This trick simplifies multiplying two numbers that are close to 100 (or 1000, etc.).","generation_guideline":"Generate a multiplication problem of two numbers that are both close to 100 (e.g., between 90-99 or 101-110).","questions":[{"id":1,"text":"Calculate $89 \\times 97$.","answer":"8633","kind":"exact","tags":["arithmetic"]},{"id":2,"text":"Calculate $96 \\times 97$.","answer":"9312","kind":"exact","tags":["arithmetic"]},{"id":3,"text":"Calculate $103 \\times 109$.","answer":"11227","kind":"exact","tags":["arithmetic"]},{"id":4,"text":"Calculate $93 \\times 97$.","answer":"9021","kind":"exact","tags":["arithmetic"]},{"id":5,"text":"Calculate $103 \\times 107$.","answer":"11021","kind":"exact","tags":["arithmetic"]},{"id":6,"text":"Calculate $93 \\times 89$.","answer":"8277","kind":"exact","tags":["arithmetic"]},{"id":7,"text":"Calculate $102 \\times 108$.","answer":"11016","kind":"exact","tags":["arithmetic"]},{"id":8,"text":"Calculate $109 \\ti